                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_474">St Albans,
                            Hertfordshire, Benedictine abbey of St Alban</orgName> <p>This
                            attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                            Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                            corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records the
                            following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an
                            attribution: in the 1635 Appendix to the Bodleian Catalogue of 1620,
                            the volume is entered as <q>Monasterii S. Albani Antiphonarium</q>, at p. 3.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance cert="low"><orgName>Church of St Andrew Undershaft, London</orgName>
                            <p>There are several obits in the calendar,
                            of the 15th and 16th centuries. One (25 June) is <q>Obitus Johannis Sawache
                            rectoris istius ecclesie</q>, which points to the church of St Andrew
                            Undershaft, London, where the rector John Savage died in 1475. <title>Medieval
                            Libraries of Great Britain</title>, 2nd edn, p. 224, rejects the identification.</provenance>
                    </history>
